## Why This Is Asked
This tests event-driven reasoning, idempotent cross-region replication, and minimal IAM in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Functions trigger on Cloud Storage finalize events
- Copy between buckets across regions, preserving path
- Idempotency via MD5 hash comparison
- Least privilege IAM and retry semantics
- Basic test plan including re-upload scenario

## Code Example
```javascript
const {Storage} = require('@google-cloud/storage');
const storage = new Storage();
const SRC = 'ingest-bucket';
const DST = 'dr-bucket';
exports.replicateToDR = async (event, context) => {
  const file = event.name;
  const srcFile = storage.bucket(SRC).file(file);
  // get MD5 from metadata
  const [md] = await srcFile.getMetadata().then(m => [m.md5Hash]);
  const dstFile = storage.bucket(DST).file(file);
  try {
    const [dstMeta] = await dstFile.getMetadata().catch(() => [null]);
    if (dstMeta && dstMeta.md5Hash === md) { return; }
    await srcFile.copy(dstFile);
  } catch (e) {
    // publish to Pub/Sub/log for alerting
    throw e;
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this for large files or many concurrent events?
- How would you monitor, alert, and test failure scenarios?

